Okay, now I'm quite confused.

Source diving reveals that minor demons are not considered demons by
the macro is_demon:

#define is_demon(ptr)           (((ptr)->mflags2 & M2_DEMON) != 0L)

But 'i' monsters have no M2_DEMON. For example imp:

    MON("imp", S_IMP,
        LVL(3, 12, 2, 20, -7), (G_GENO|1),
        A(ATTK(AT_CLAW, AD_PHYS, 1, 4),
          NO_ATTK, NO_ATTK, NO_ATTK, NO_ATTK, NO_ATTK),
        SIZ(20, 10, 0, MS_CUSS, MZ_TINY), 0, 0,
        M1_REGEN, M2_WANDER|M2_STALK, M3_INFRAVISIBLE|M3_INFRAVISION, CLR_RED),

Likewise Demonbane does only double damage against M2_DEMON monsters
if I'm reading the code correctly.

> Sometimes not using tiles is advantageous.

I'm not using tiles.

I was misled by the way vampires act in NetHack. They act like those
vampire in literature and tv that are demons.

But in NetHack vampires are "only" undead.

